cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MiraProt in your research, please cite the software and the associated publication."
title: "MiraProt"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"

authors:
  - family-names: "Schmalen"
given-names: "Adrian"

abstract: >-
  MiraProt is an R Shiny-based platform for integrated downstream proteomics
analysis. It connects multiple analysis workflows, including differential
expression analysis, dimensionality reduction, functional enrichment,
gene-set enrichment analysis, protein interaction network analysis, and
visualization within a modular interactive application.

repository-code: "https://github.com/AdSchmalen/MiraProt"

license: MIT

keywords:
  - proteomics
- bioinformatics
- R
- Shiny
- differential expression
- principal component analysis
- gene set enrichment analysis
- functional enrichment
- protein interaction networks
- research software